Detect the Kubernetes distribution and check that the registry service, cluster DNS, operator/CRD prerequisites, ingress (Traefik) wiring, image pulls, Sentinel, and MCPServer reconciliation are healthy. Prints remediation steps for your distribution when something is missing. Use --for-setup before setup for cluster prerequisites, or --after-setup after setup for the complete installed-platform validation. With no lifecycle flag, the command keeps the complete post-setup behavior for backward compatibility. See docs/cluster-readiness.md for the full per-distribution checklist.

Usage:
  mcp-runtime cluster doctor [flags]

Flags:
      --after-setup         Run the complete post-setup validation for installed Runtime components
      --for-setup           Run pre-setup readiness checks for ingress, public DNS, and TLS prerequisites
  -h, --help                help for doctor
      --kubeconfig string   Path to kubeconfig file (auto-detects ~/.kube/config or /etc/rancher/k3s/k3s.yaml)

Global Flags:
      --debug   Enable debug mode with structured error logging
